  "deviations": [
    "IDs were not renumbered. On main d6fa6e2a the highest TRACE id was BGS-TRACE-148, so 149 was the next free id. Gaps 138 and 139 were left unused, as when Line C was numbered from 143. The Line B packet had not merged, so no Line B claim id was added as a dependency. The packet sentences that called the ids provisional were updated to record that confirmation.",
    "record/claims.json source fields are the note path without the #claim-NNN fragment. scientific_registry_audit.require_path requires an existing file, and the atlas generator keys claims by that exact path. The anchors remain in the note.",
    "The four open claims gained closure_condition, copied from the note's own closure sentences. The registry auditor rejects an open claim without one. No state was changed.",
    "d8_spot.py and lean_semantics.py no longer read /workspace/bgs-lineD. The two paths are resolved from the script directory, as REFEREE_STATUS.md required before replay.",
    "linec_exact.py still imports computations/verification/lineC/gauss_exact.py via ../../lineC from computations/verification/lineD/code. An existence check was added, and the JSON log is written next to the script rather than relative to the process cwd.",
    "The repository build is a full lake build Bgs after lake exe cache get. The packet built only Bgs.LineDCerts. This cache reported 8690 decompressed files; the packet log reported 8689.",
    "Every Line D Python file carries the repository assertion-entry guard. Under ordinary Python the guard is a no-op. It is required so assertion-bearing verifiers refuse to run when assertions are disabled.",
    "The generated atlas row uses the note's H1 and is ordered alphabetically, so it precedes the Line C row. The claim ids and states match GENERATED_SURFACES.md. STATUS counts match that note: 246 claims, proved 209, verification-pending 15, conditional 10, open 12.",
    "Pandoc 3.12.1 and pdflatex are not installed here, so the three TeX sync --check scripts and the unified PDF build were not run. audit_manuscript_references.py --check passed. GitHub Actions was not executed.",
    "bibliographic_metadata_audit.py --self-test and the Wave2 portable source seal fail on this tree for reasons already present on main d6fa6e2a (EXT-BR-1975's recorded impact omits BGS-TRACE-116; mathematics/fixed-map/position_chain_mixing.md does not match the sealed digest). Those files were not edited. The assertion-policy unit tests still fail on 13 pre-existing scripts outside lineD."
  ],
